1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,700
Claude has now become insanely good

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:03,220
at motion graphics and video editing,

3
00:00:03,339 --> 00:00:04,919
but the sound effects that ads still suck.

4
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:07,080
To fix that, use these three free tools

5
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,880
that add professional sounds to your timeline

6
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,560
at the right place and the right level,

7
00:00:10,699 --> 00:00:11,740
just like a pro editor would.

8
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:13,400
The first is OpenVerse API,

9
00:00:13,619 --> 00:00:14,820
which gives your AI agent access

10
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:16,839
to over five million high quality sound effects

11
00:00:16,839 --> 00:00:18,320
that it can search and download on its own.

12
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:19,839
The second is Real SFX,

13
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,059
which studies your timeline,

14
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,839
finds each moment that needs a sound

15
00:00:22,839 --> 00:00:24,460
and adds one at the exact frame.

16
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:25,820
And finally, if it still can't find

17
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:26,600
the right sound effect,

18
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:29,460
use Earshot to generate a brand new one in code,

19
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,379
or even a whole sound kit that fits your project.

20
00:00:31,579 --> 00:00:32,500
So if you want all three of these,

21
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:33,780
just comment sound down below

22
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:34,899
and I'll send you the links directly.
